  "confidence": "low",
  "note": "The adapter itself has no controls. Only the throttle handle is placed on the inset; the TQS switches are tiny grey caps on a blurry ~15% inset, so which cap is which cannot be told from this photo. The two knurled grey parts at the grip front are the ANT ELEV wheel and the MAN RNG knob, but which is which is not certain: hidden candidates. Idle/Mil/Afterburner areas and the COMMS centre are throttle positions / switch centres generated by the adapter, not separate controls. Axis names: the FSSB-R3 User Guide p.101 (https://www.realsimulator.com/download/FSSB-R3_User_Guide.pdf) lists the TUSBA axes as JOY_X cursor X, JOY_Y cursor Y, JOY_Z range, JOY_RX antenna elevation, JOY_RY throttle, JOY_RZ idle, JOY_S1 mil, JOY_S2 afterburner (catalog says the axis names are not documented).",
